From b8ff6422ef9055e22431a0e3bd8ede0c77472c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kgvarunkanth <kgvarunkanth@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:06:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] mido: label Unbound binaries under /system/system_ext too

On mido system_ext is a directory of system, so init saw system_file and
refused to start the services.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/private/file_contexts | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sepolicy/private/file_contexts b/sepolicy/private/file_contexts
index f453d6a..312aaa2 100644
--- a/sepolicy/private/file_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/private/file_contexts
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
-/system_ext/bin/unbound             u:object_r:kgv_unbound_exec:s0
-/system_ext/bin/kgv_dns_redirect    u:object_r:kgv_dns_exec:s0
-/data/misc/kgv_unbound(/.*)?        u:object_r:kgv_unbound_data_file:s0
+/(system_ext|system/system_ext)/bin/unbound             u:object_r:kgv_unbound_exec:s0
+/(system_ext|system/system_ext)/bin/kgv_dns_redirect    u:object_r:kgv_dns_exec:s0
+/data/misc/kgv_unbound(/.*)?                            u:object_r:kgv_unbound_data_file:s0
-- 
2.53.0

